WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.840
When you register as a professional seller in the US, Canada, or Mexico, you'll automatically

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:17.560
have access to all of Amazon's North American marketplaces from a single account, making it

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:23.400
that much easier to introduce your product offers to a new pool of international customers.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.300
This is called the North America Unified Account.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.200
If you register as an individual seller in

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:35.080
the US or Canada, you'll still have access to both of those countries, but not Mexico.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:39.880
The North America Unified Account lets you create and manage product offers, tailor your

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:45.560
listings, and manage pricing and inventory across the US, Canada, and Mexico marketplaces

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.448
from a single interface.

00:00:47.448 --> 00:00:50.752
To quickly list your inventory across Amazon.

00:00:50.752 --> 00:00:51.696
com, Amazon.

00:00:51.696 --> 00:00:52.640
ca, and

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:53.148
Amazon.

00:00:53.148 --> 00:00:53.656
com.

00:00:53.656 --> 00:00:59.752
mx, locate the Expand Internationally Widget on the Seller Central home page.

00:00:59.752 --> 00:01:00.260
Click

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.946
on Enable More Listings.

00:01:01.946 --> 00:01:05.739
That'll take you to the Build International Listings tab.

00:01:05.739 --> 00:01:06.160
Choose

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:11.240
your source marketplace, then click Connect Listings for each target marketplace in which

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:12.720
you wish to sell.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:17.160
Select the target marketplace, offer type, and the pricing rules for your

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.000
listings, then click Save.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:23.140
With that, all eligible listings in the source marketplace

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:29.080
will be listed in the target marketplace, connected using the pricing rule you selected.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:33.440
Once you've connected your listings, you can exclude specific products from being listed

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:38.304
in the target marketplace, or adjust your pricing rules at any time.

00:01:38.304 --> 00:01:39.520
Remember, you should

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.400
review and verify the listing information for each product you intend to sell in Canada

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:49.167
and Mexico, and exclude any offers for products you don't intend to sell.

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:51.000
Not all of the products

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.612
you offer in the US may be appropriate for sale in Canada or Mexico.

00:01:55.612 --> 00:01:56.600
Be certain each

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:02.240
product you list complies with all applicable laws, regulations, and Amazon policies before

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.440
you offer it for sale.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.520
For more information about North America Unified

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:14.520
Accounts, search "North America Marketplaces" in Seller Central Help.
